(window.STEP_BOOK = window.STEP_BOOK || {})["C1"] = {"n":1,"level":"A1","t":"Building Sentences and Simple Paragraphs","lessons":[{"id":"1.1","t":"The Sentence: Capital Letters, Full Stops, Subject + Verb","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.1 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Write complete sentences with a capital letter, a subject, a verb and a full stop.</p>\n<p>2. Find a missing subject or verb in a sentence.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يكتب الطالب جملًا كاملة تبدأ بحرف كبير وتحتوي على فاعل وفعل وتنتهي بنقطة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يكتشف الفاعل أو الفعل الناقص في الجملة.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>A sentence is a group of words that gives one complete idea. Every English sentence needs two things: a SUBJECT (who or what the sentence is about) and a VERB (what the subject does or is). In 'Ali plays football', Ali is the subject and plays is the verb.</p>\n<p>Every sentence starts with a capital letter and ends with a full stop (.), a question mark (?) or an exclamation mark (!). Some words ALWAYS start with a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence: the word I, names of people (Sara), cities and countries (Jeddah, Saudi Arabia), days and months (Friday, March), languages (English, Arabic) and names of schools and places (Al-Noor School).</p>\n<p>Arabic speakers often leave out the verb be (am, is, are) because Arabic does not need it: 'My father a doctor' is wrong; the correct sentence is 'My father is a doctor.' Arabic speakers also sometimes drop the subject: 'Is very hot today' is wrong; the correct sentence is 'It is very hot today.' In STEP, many error items test these two problems.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>✓</strong> My brother is a teacher. (subject: My brother · verb: is)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> my brother is a teacher. → My brother is a teacher. (capital letter at the start)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> My brother a teacher. → My brother is a teacher. (missing verb is)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Is very cold today. → It is very cold today. (missing subject It)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Last week, visited my uncle. → Last week, we visited my uncle. (missing subject)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> We go to the beach on friday. → We go to the beach on Friday. (days have capitals)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> My friend and i live in taif. → My friend and I live in Taif. (I and city names)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Because it was raining. → We stayed at home because it was raining. (not a complete idea)</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة مجموعة كلمات تعطي فكرة كاملة، وتحتاج دائمًا إلى فاعل وفعل، وتبدأ بحرف كبير وتنتهي بنقطة أو علامة استفهام أو تعجب. وتبدأ بعض الكلمات بحرف كبير دائمًا: الضمير I وأسماء الأشخاص والمدن والدول والأيام والشهور واللغات والمدارس. ويحذف الطالب العربي أحيانًا فعل الكينونة (is / am / are) لأن العربية لا تحتاجه، أو يحذف الفاعل مثل Is very hot والصحيح It is very hot.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Find the verb first. If there is no verb, the sentence is not complete.</p>\n<p>2. Ask: Who or what does the verb? That is the subject. If there is no subject, add one (I, it, we, they).</p>\n<p>3. Check the first letter of the sentence and the word I.</p>\n<p>4. Check names, cities, days, months and languages for capital letters.</p>\n<p>5. Check the end mark: a question needs a question mark.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث عن الفعل أولًا، ثم اسأل من قام بالفعل لتجد الفاعل، وتحقق من الحرف الأول في الجملة ومن الضمير I، ومن أسماء الأشخاص والمدن والأيام والشهور واللغات، ومن علامة نهاية الجملة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ A capital letter in the wrong place (my Uncle, In Dammam).</p>\n<p>✗ A group of words that starts with Because or When and has no main idea.</p>\n<p>✗ A sentence without am / is / are (My sister happy).</p>\n<p>✗ A sentence that starts with a verb and has no subject (Likes football very much).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. (A) <u>my</u> (B) <u>brother</u> (C) <u>is</u> a (D) <u>doctor</u> in Riyadh.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. my B. brother C. is D. doctor</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Read the whole sentence: subject (brother) + verb (is) are there.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Check the first letter: my starts with a small letter.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is A: it should be My.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الخطأ في A لأن الجملة يجب أن تبدأ بحرف كبير.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which group of words is a complete sentence?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. The late bus today. B. Is late today.</p>\n<p>C. Because the bus is late. D. The bus is late today.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Look for a subject and a verb in each option.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'The late bus today' has no verb; 'Is late today' has no subject; 'Because the bus is late' is not a complete idea.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only 'The bus is late today' is complete.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث عن الفاعل والفعل في كل بديل، وتذكّر أن الجملة التي تبدأ بـ Because وحدها ليست كاملة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. (A) <u>Last</u> summer, (B) <u>visited</u> my (C) <u>grandparents</u> (D) <u>in</u> Abha.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Last B. visited C. grandparents D. in</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Find the verb: visited.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Ask: Who visited? There is no subject.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B: add a subject (I visited).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفعل visited بلا فاعل، فالخطأ في B.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-A1-01 — My school day in five sentences</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write five sentences (40–60 words) about your school day. Every sentence must have a capital letter, a subject, a verb and a full stop.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب خمس جمل (من أربعين إلى ستين كلمة) عن يومك الدراسي، وتأكد من أن كل جملة تبدأ بحرف كبير وفيها فاعل وفعل وتنتهي بنقطة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Sentence 1: Who are you and where do you study?</p>\n<p>2. Sentence 2: When do you wake up?</p>\n<p>3. Sentence 3: How do you go to school?</p>\n<p>4. Sentence 4: What is your favourite lesson?</p>\n<p>5. Sentence 5: What do you do after school?</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (47 words; target 40–60)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I am a student at Al-Andalus School in Taif. I wake up at six o'clock every day. My father drives me to school at seven. I have six lessons, and English is my favourite subject. After school, I eat lunch with my family and do my homework.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ Every sentence starts with a capital letter and ends with a full stop.</p>\n<p>▸ Each sentence has a subject (I, My father, English) and a verb (am, wake up, drives, is, eat).</p>\n<p>▸ Names (Al-Andalus School, Taif, English) have capital letters.</p>\n<p>▸ The sentences follow the order of the day, so the paragraph is easy to read.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Does every sentence start with a capital letter?</p>\n<p>☐ Does every sentence have a subject and a verb?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I use is / am / are where I need them?</p>\n<p>☐ Do names, cities, days and languages have capital letters?</p>\n<p>☐ Does every sentence end with a full stop?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">راجع كل جملة: هل تبدأ بحرف كبير؟ هل فيها فاعل وفعل؟ هل أسماء الأماكن والأيام واللغات تبدأ بحرف كبير؟ هل تنتهي بنقطة؟</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 A · Example 2 D · Example 3 B","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence is written correctly?","o":["my name is Ali.","My name is ali.","My name is Ali.","My name Ali."],"k":2,"e":"[error] My name is Ali. — Capital M at the start, capital A in the name, and the verb is.","h":"حرف كبير في البداية وفي الاسم مع الفعل is."},{"n":2,"s":"(A) we (B) go to school (C) at seven (D) o'clock.","o":["we","go","at","o'clock"],"k":0,"e":"[error] we — The first word needs a capital letter: We.","h":"أول كلمة تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"n":3,"s":"Which group of words is a complete sentence?","o":["The cat on the sofa.","Sleeps on the sofa.","The cat sleeps on the sofa.","On the sofa every day."],"k":2,"e":"[error] The cat sleeps on the sofa. — It has a subject (The cat) and a verb (sleeps).","h":"فيها فاعل وفعل."},{"n":4,"s":"My brother (A) and I (B) play football (C) in the park every (D) friday.","o":["and","play","in","friday"],"k":3,"e":"[error] friday — Days of the week start with a capital letter: Friday.","h":"أيام الأسبوع تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence has a subject and a verb?","o":["A book for Sara.","Reads a book every night.","Sara and her book.","Sara reads a book."],"k":3,"e":"[error] Sara reads a book. — Sara is the subject and reads is the verb.","h":"Sara فاعل وreads فعل."},{"n":6,"s":"(A) Every morning, (B) drinks milk (C) with (D) my breakfast.","o":["Every","drinks","with","my"],"k":1,"e":"[error] drinks — There is no subject; it should be 'I drink'.","h":"الجملة بلا فاعل."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence begins correctly?","o":["Riyadh is a big city.","riyadh is a big city.","Is a big city Riyadh.","riyadh a big city."],"k":0,"e":"[error] Riyadh is a big city. — Capital R, subject first, then the verb is.","h":"حرف كبير ثم الفاعل ثم الفعل."},{"n":8,"s":"Ahmed (A) is (B) from (C) jeddah, and he (D) likes the sea.","o":["is","from","jeddah","likes"],"k":2,"e":"[error] jeddah — City names start with a capital letter: Jeddah.","h":"أسماء المدن تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence ends correctly?","o":["Where do you live.","where do you live?","Where do you live?","Where do you live,"],"k":2,"e":"[error] Where do you live? — A question starts with a capital letter and ends with a question mark.","h":"السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"n":10,"s":"My friends and (A) i (B) like (C) pizza very (D) much.","o":["i","like","pizza","much"],"k":0,"e":"[error] i — The word I is always a capital letter.","h":"الضمير I يُكتب دائمًا بحرف كبير."},{"n":11,"s":"Which group of words is NOT a complete sentence?","o":["It was raining.","We stayed at home.","My father drove us.","Because it was raining."],"k":3,"e":"[error] Because it was raining. — A group of words that starts with Because needs a main idea, e.g. We stayed at home because it was raining.","h":"العبارة التي تبدأ بـ Because وحدها ليست جملة كاملة."},{"n":12,"s":"(A) Last week, (B) visited my (C) grandmother (D) in Abha.","o":["Last","visited","grandmother","in"],"k":1,"e":"[error] visited — The verb visited has no subject; it should be 'we visited'.","h":"الفعل بلا فاعل."},{"n":13,"s":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["The children in the garden.","The children are in the garden.","the children are in the garden.","Are in the garden the children."],"k":1,"e":"[error] The children are in the garden. — Capital T, subject (The children) and verb (are).","h":"حرف كبير وفاعل وفعل."},{"n":14,"s":"(A) Our school (B) has a library, (C) and (D) it very quiet.","o":["Our","has","and","it very"],"k":3,"e":"[error] it very — The verb is is missing: it is very quiet.","h":"ينقص الفعل is."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence uses capital letters correctly?","o":["my Uncle lives in Dammam.","My uncle lives in Dammam.","My uncle Lives in dammam.","My Uncle lives In Dammam."],"k":1,"e":"[error] My uncle lives in Dammam. — Only the first word and the city name need capitals.","h":"الحرف الكبير في أول الجملة واسم المدينة فقط."},{"n":16,"s":"In the (A) evening, my (B) father (C) reading the (D) newspaper.","o":["evening","father","reading","newspaper"],"k":2,"e":"[error] reading — reading alone is not a full verb; it should be 'reads' or 'is reading'.","h":"reading وحدها ليست فعلًا كاملًا."},{"n":17,"s":"Which group of words is a complete sentence?","o":["Every Saturday, we visit the market.","Every Saturday at the market.","Visit the market every Saturday.","Every Saturday, the market near our house."],"k":0,"e":"[error] Every Saturday, we visit the market. — It has a subject (we) and a verb (visit).","h":"فيها فاعل وفعل."},{"n":18,"s":"Fahad and his brother (A) are (B) in the same class at (C) the (D) al-noor school.","o":["are","in","the","al-noor school"],"k":3,"e":"[error] al-noor school — School names start with capital letters: Al-Noor School.","h":"أسماء المدارس تبدأ بحروف كبيرة."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["It is hot in July.","Is hot in July.","It hot in July.","it is hot in july."],"k":0,"e":"[error] It is hot in July. — It (subject) + is (verb), with capital letters for It and July.","h":"الفاعل It والفعل is وحرف كبير لاسم الشهر."},{"n":20,"s":"My (A) favourite subject (B) is English (C) because (D) is easy and fun.","o":["favourite","is","because","is"],"k":3,"e":"[error] is — The second part has no subject: it should be 'it is easy'.","h":"الجزء الثاني بلا فاعل."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) My school bag is blue. (2) It has three pockets. (3) I keep my books in the big pocket. (4) My cousin has a new bicycle. (5) My pens are in the small pocket."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The paragraph is about the school bag; the cousin's bicycle is a different topic.","h":"الجملة عن دراجة ابن العم لا عن الحقيبة."},{"n":22,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["and","so","because","but"],"x":["I like apples, ______ I don't like bananas."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] but — but joins two different ideas (like / don't like).","h":"but للتضاد."},{"n":23,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","1 – 2 – 4 – 3","2 – 1 – 3 – 4"],"x":["(1) Then I eat breakfast.","(2) I wake up at six o'clock.","(3) Finally, I go to school by bus.","(4) After breakfast, I brush my teeth."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 1 – 4 – 3 — Wake up → Then breakfast → After breakfast, teeth → Finally, school.","h":"رتّب الأحداث حسب الزمن."},{"n":24,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My friend has a big car.","I like football very much.","The weather is cold today.","I live in a small house."],"x":["______ It is small but very beautiful. It has a garden with many flowers. My family loves our home."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] I live in a small house. — The paragraph is about a house, so the topic sentence must introduce the house.","h":"الفقرة عن البيت."},{"n":25,"s":"(A) My sister (B) are (C) ten years (D) old.","o":["My","are","ten","old"],"k":1,"e":"[error] are — My sister is singular, so the verb is is: My sister is ten.","h":"الفاعل مفرد فالفعل is."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My grandparents live in Taif.","That is why Friday is my favourite day.","Mondays are very busy.","I have a new computer game."],"x":["I love Fridays. On Friday, my family goes to the mosque. After lunch, we visit my grandparents. In the evening, we play games together. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] That is why Friday is my favourite day. — The conclusion repeats the main idea: Friday is a favourite day.","h":"الخاتمة تعيد الفكرة الرئيسة."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["He is always helpful.","He has a sister.","Maths is on Sunday.","I don't like maths."],"x":["My best friend is Khalid. He is in my class. ______ For example, he helps me with maths. He is a very good friend."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] He is always helpful. — 'For example, he helps me' needs a sentence about being helpful before it.","h":"المثال يحتاج جملة عن المساعدة قبله."},{"n":28,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["but","so","or","because"],"x":["It was very cold, ______ I wore my jacket."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] so — so shows a result: cold → jacket.","h":"so للنتيجة."},{"n":29,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Camels are very useful animals. (2) They can walk for days without water. (3) People use their milk for food. (4) My favourite colour is green. (5) Camels can carry heavy things. (6) That is why people love camels."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — All sentences are about camels except the favourite colour.","h":"الجملة عن اللون المفضل لا عن الجمال."},{"n":30,"s":"Yesterday, (A) my friends (B) and I (C) go to the (D) park.","o":["my","and","go","park"],"k":2,"e":"[error] go — Yesterday needs the past tense: went.","h":"Yesterday تحتاج الماضي went."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.2","t":"Word Order in Simple Sentences","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.2 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Put words in the correct order in simple sentences.</p>\n<p>2. Correct word-order errors carried over from Arabic.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يرتب الطالب الكلمات ترتيبًا صحيحًا في الجمل البسيطة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يصحح أخطاء ترتيب الكلمات المنقولة من العربية.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>English sentences follow a fixed order: SUBJECT + VERB + OBJECT + PLACE + TIME. For example: My brother (subject) plays (verb) football (object) in the park (place) every evening (time). Changing this order often makes the sentence wrong or hard to understand.</p>\n<p>Some words have special places. Adjectives come BEFORE the noun: a red car, a big house, a difficult test (not a car red). Frequency adverbs (always, usually, often, never) come BEFORE the main verb but AFTER am / is / are: I always walk to school; She is never late. The words very much come at the END: I like chocolate very much.</p>\n<p>Questions change the order. With be, the verb comes before the subject: Is your house big? With other verbs, we add do / does / did: Where do you live? (not Where you live?). Arabic speakers often put the adjective after the noun or the verb before the subject, because that is the Arabic order. STEP tests these mistakes in error items and best-order items.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>✓</strong> My father reads the newspaper every morning. (subject – verb – object – time)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> We have a car white. → We have a white car. (adjective before the noun)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Plays my brother football. → My brother plays football. (subject before the verb)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> I go always to the mosque. → I always go to the mosque. (always before the main verb)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> I like very much pizza. → I like pizza very much. (very much at the end)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Where you live? → Where do you live? (question with do)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> She is late never. → She is never late. (never after is)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Every Friday to the beach we go. → We go to the beach every Friday. (place, then time)</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ترتيب الجملة الإنجليزية ثابت: الفاعل ثم الفعل ثم المفعول ثم المكان ثم الزمان. والصفة تأتي قبل الاسم (a red car)، وظروف التكرار مثل always وnever تأتي قبل الفعل الرئيس وبعد am / is / are، وعبارة very much تأتي في آخر الجملة. وفي الأسئلة نضع الفعل المساعد قبل الفاعل (Where do you live?). ويخطئ الطالب العربي عندما يضع الصفة بعد الاسم أو الفعل قبل الفاعل كما في العربية.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Find the subject and the verb, and put them first.</p>\n<p>2. Check every adjective: it must come before its noun.</p>\n<p>3. Check always, usually, often and never: before the main verb, after am / is / are.</p>\n<p>4. Put place before time at the end of the sentence.</p>\n<p>5. In questions, check for do / does / did or for be before the subject.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ضع الفاعل ثم الفعل أولًا، وتحقق من أن كل صفة قبل اسمها، وأن ظروف التكرار قبل الفعل الرئيس، وأن المكان قبل الزمان في آخر الجملة، وأن السؤال فيه do أو does أو did أو فعل be قبل الفاعل.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ The Arabic order with the adjective after the noun (a house big).</p>\n<p>✗ A verb before the subject (Likes my sister cats).</p>\n<p>✗ very much in the middle of the sentence.</p>\n<p>✗ A question without do / does (What you want?).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Choose the best order for the sentences.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>(1)</strong> at school</p>\n<p><strong>(2)</strong> I</p>\n<p><strong>(3)</strong> English</p>\n<p><strong>(4)</strong> study</p>\n<p>A. 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 B. 4 – 2 – 3 – 1 C. 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 D. 2 – 4 – 3 – 1</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Find the subject: I. Find the verb: study.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The object comes after the verb: English. The place comes last: at school.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The best order is 2 – 4 – 3 – 1: I study English at school.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">رتّب: فاعل ثم فعل ثم مفعول ثم مكان.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. We (A) <u>have</u> (B) <u>a garden</u> (C) <u>beautiful</u> (D) <u>behind</u> our house.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. have B. a garden C. beautiful D. behind</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Look at the noun garden and its adjective beautiful.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> In English, the adjective goes before the noun.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is C: it should be 'a beautiful garden'.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الصفة beautiful يجب أن تأتي قبل الاسم garden.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence has the correct word order?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. My uncle has a car white. B. Has my uncle a white car.</p>\n<p>C. My uncle has a white car. D. My uncle a white car has.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Check the subject and the verb: My uncle has.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Check the adjective: white must come before car.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only 'My uncle has a white car' is correct.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث عن الترتيب: فاعل ثم فعل ثم صفة ثم اسم.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-A1-02 — Describing my bedroom</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Describe your bedroom in 40–60 words. Use at least four adjectives before nouns and the phrases there is / there are.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">صف غرفة نومك في أربعين إلى ستين كلمة، واستخدم أربع صفات على الأقل قبل الأسماء والعبارتين there is وthere are.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Sentence 1: Is your room big or small?</p>\n<p>2. Sentences 2–3: What furniture is there? (There is … / There are …)</p>\n<p>3. Sentence 4: What colour are the things in your room?</p>\n<p>4. Sentence 5: Where do you keep your books?</p>\n<p>5. Sentence 6: How do you keep your room?</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (45 words; target 40–60)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My bedroom is small but comfortable. There is a big bed near the window. I have a brown desk and a blue chair. My books are on a white shelf. There are two pictures on the wall. I always keep my room clean and tidy.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ All adjectives come before their nouns: big bed, brown desk, blue chair, white shelf.</p>\n<p>▸ There is is used with one thing and there are with two pictures.</p>\n<p>▸ The frequency adverb always is in the right place: I always keep.</p>\n<p>▸ Each sentence follows subject + verb + object + place.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Did I put every adjective before its noun?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I use there is for one thing and there are for many things?</p>\n<p>☐ Are always / usually / never before the main verb?</p>\n<p>☐ Does every sentence start with a subject and a verb?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I use capital letters and full stops?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من أن الصفات قبل الأسماء، ومن استخدام there is للمفرد وthere are للجمع، ومن موضع always قبل الفعل.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 D · Example 2 C · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence has the correct word order?","o":["I have a car red.","I a red car have.","Have I a car red.","I have a red car."],"k":3,"e":"[error] I have a red car. — Subject + verb + adjective + noun.","h":"الصفة قبل الاسم."},{"n":2,"s":"We (A) live in a (B) house big (C) near the (D) mosque.","o":["live","house big","near","mosque"],"k":1,"e":"[error] house big — The adjective comes before the noun: a big house.","h":"الصفة قبل الاسم."},{"n":3,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1"],"x":["(1) football","(2) My brother","(3) every evening","(4) plays"],"k":2,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — My brother plays football every evening: subject, verb, object, time.","h":"فاعل ثم فعل ثم مفعول ثم زمن."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence has the correct word order?","o":["She drinks always tea in the morning.","She always drinks tea in the morning.","Drinks she always tea in the morning.","She always tea drinks in the morning."],"k":1,"e":"[error] She always drinks tea in the morning. — always comes before the main verb drinks.","h":"always قبل الفعل الرئيس."},{"n":5,"s":"(A) Plays my brother (B) football (C) with his (D) friends.","o":["Plays","football","with","friends"],"k":0,"e":"[error] Plays — The subject comes before the verb: My brother plays football.","h":"الفاعل قبل الفعل."},{"n":6,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 1 – 4 – 2","4 – 1 – 3 – 2","3 – 1 – 2 – 4","3 – 4 – 1 – 2"],"x":["(1) you","(2) live","(3) Where","(4) do"],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 3 – 4 – 1 – 2 — Where do you live? Question word + do + subject + verb.","h":"أداة الاستفهام ثم do ثم الفاعل ثم الفعل."},{"n":7,"s":"Which question is correct?","o":["What your name is?","Your name what is?","What name your is?","What is your name?"],"k":3,"e":"[error] What is your name? — Question word + is + subject.","h":"أداة الاستفهام ثم is ثم الفاعل."},{"n":8,"s":"I (A) like (B) very much (C) chocolate (D) cake.","o":["like","very much","chocolate","cake"],"k":1,"e":"[error] very much — very much goes at the end: I like chocolate cake very much.","h":"very much في آخر الجملة."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["The man tall is my teacher.","Tall the man is my teacher.","The tall is man my teacher.","The tall man is my teacher."],"k":3,"e":"[error] The tall man is my teacher. — The adjective tall comes before man.","h":"الصفة قبل الاسم."},{"n":10,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 1 – 4 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","1 – 2 – 4 – 3"],"x":["(1) to the park","(2) We","(3) on Saturday","(4) go"],"k":2,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — We go to the park on Saturday: subject, verb, place, time.","h":"المكان قبل الزمان."},{"n":11,"s":"My mother (A) makes (B) a cake (C) delicious (D) every Friday.","o":["makes","a cake","delicious","every Friday"],"k":2,"e":"[error] delicious — The adjective comes before the noun: a delicious cake.","h":"الصفة قبل الاسم."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence has the correct word order?","o":["There is a big tree in our garden.","There is a tree big in our garden.","In our garden a big tree there is.","A big tree there is in our garden."],"k":0,"e":"[error] There is a big tree in our garden. — There is + adjective + noun + place.","h":"There is ثم الصفة ثم الاسم ثم المكان."},{"n":13,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["1 – 2 – 4 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","2 – 1 – 4 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3"],"x":["(1) usually","(2) I","(3) at seven","(4) have breakfast"],"k":2,"e":"[best order] 2 – 1 – 4 – 3 — I usually have breakfast at seven: usually before the main verb.","h":"usually قبل الفعل."},{"n":14,"s":"My (A) cousin has (B) two (C) cats white and a (D) small dog.","o":["cousin","two","cats white","small"],"k":2,"e":"[error] cats white — The adjective comes before the noun: two white cats.","h":"الصفة قبل الاسم."},{"n":15,"s":"Which question is correct?","o":["You like fish do?","Do you like fish?","Like you fish?","Do like you fish?"],"k":1,"e":"[error] Do you like fish? — Do + subject + verb.","h":"Do ثم الفاعل ثم الفعل."},{"n":16,"s":"(A) Always my grandmother (B) tells us (C) interesting (D) stories.","o":["Always","tells","interesting","stories"],"k":0,"e":"[error] Always — always goes before the main verb: My grandmother always tells us stories.","h":"always قبل الفعل الرئيس."},{"n":17,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["1 – 2 – 4 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","3 – 1 – 2 – 4","2 – 1 – 4 – 3"],"x":["(1) is","(2) The weather","(3) today","(4) very hot"],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 2 – 1 – 4 – 3 — The weather is very hot today.","h":"الفاعل ثم الفعل ثم الصفة ثم الزمن."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence has the correct word order?","o":["My friend speaks very well English.","My friend speaks English very well.","My friend very well speaks English.","Very well my friend English speaks."],"k":1,"e":"[error] My friend speaks English very well. — very well comes after the object English.","h":"very well بعد المفعول."},{"n":19,"s":"Our teacher (A) gave (B) us (C) homework difficult (D) yesterday.","o":["gave","us","homework difficult","yesterday"],"k":2,"e":"[error] homework difficult — The adjective comes before the noun: difficult homework.","h":"الصفة قبل الاسم."},{"n":20,"s":"Which question has the correct word order?","o":["How many brothers you have?","How many brothers do you have?","How many do you have brothers?","You have how many brothers?"],"k":1,"e":"[error] How many brothers do you have? — How many + noun + do + subject + verb.","h":"How many ثم الاسم ثم do ثم الفاعل ثم الفعل."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["because","but","or","so"],"x":["I stayed at home ______ I was sick."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] because — because gives the reason: I was sick.","h":"because للسبب."},{"n":22,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) My room is small but nice. (2) There is a bed near the window. (3) I have a desk for my homework. (4) My uncle works at the airport. (5) I keep my books on a shelf."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The paragraph describes the room; the uncle's job is off the topic.","h":"الجملة عن عمل العم لا عن الغرفة."},{"n":23,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 3 – 4","1 – 2 – 3 – 4","2 – 3 – 1 – 4","2 – 1 – 4 – 3"],"x":["(1) Next, she put the cake in the oven.","(2) First, my mother mixed eggs, sugar and flour.","(3) After forty minutes, the cake was ready.","(4) We ate it together after dinner."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 1 – 3 – 4 — First → Next → After forty minutes → after dinner.","h":"رتّب حسب كلمات التسلسل."},{"n":24,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My school starts at seven.","Riyadh is very hot in summer.","I have a new phone.","My family loves visiting Abha."],"x":["______ We go there every summer. The weather is cool, and the mountains are green. We walk and have picnics."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] My family loves visiting Abha. — The paragraph describes summer visits to a cool, green place.","h":"الفقرة عن زيارة أبها."},{"n":25,"s":"There (A) are (B) a big (C) supermarket (D) near my house.","o":["are","a","supermarket","near"],"k":0,"e":"[error] are — One supermarket needs there is.","h":"المفرد يحتاج there is."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My grandmother likes flowers.","The mosque is near the market.","He is old, but he is very active.","I get up at seven."],"x":["My grandfather is seventy years old. He gets up early every day. He walks to the mosque and reads the Quran. He also helps my grandmother in the garden. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] He is old, but he is very active. — The conclusion sums up the paragraph: an old but active grandfather.","h":"الخاتمة تلخص الفكرة."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["His name is Sunny, and he is yellow.","My brother has a cat.","Birds can fly very high.","I don't like dogs."],"x":["I have a pet bird. ______ He sings every morning. I give him seeds and water every day."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] His name is Sunny, and he is yellow. — The missing sentence introduces the bird, which the next sentences describe.","h":"الجملة تعرّف بالطائر."},{"n":28,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["but","or","so","because"],"x":["Do you want tea ______ coffee?"],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] or — or offers a choice.","h":"or للاختيار."},{"n":29,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Dates are a popular food in Saudi Arabia. (2) There are many kinds of dates. (3) People eat them with Arabic coffee. (4) Dates are healthy and sweet. (5) Football is a popular sport. (6) Many families have dates at home every day."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — All the sentences are about dates except the one about football.","h":"الجملة عن كرة القدم لا عن التمر."},{"n":30,"s":"My father (A) work (B) in a hospital (C) in (D) Riyadh.","o":["work","in","in","Riyadh"],"k":0,"e":"[error] work — My father is singular: works.","h":"الفاعل مفرد فالفعل works."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.3","t":"Joining Ideas: and, but, or, because, so","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.3 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Join two ideas with the correct conjunction.</p>\n<p>2. Choose the best connector for a short text.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يربط الطالب بين فكرتين بأداة الربط المناسبة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختار أداة الربط الأنسب في نص قصير.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>Conjunctions join two ideas into one sentence. Each one has a different meaning. AND adds a similar idea (I like tea and coffee). BUT shows a contrast or a surprise (I like tea, but I don't like coffee). OR gives a choice (Do you want tea or coffee?).</p>\n<p>BECAUSE gives a reason: it answers the question Why? (I stayed at home because I was ill.) SO gives a result: it tells us what happened next (I was ill, so I stayed at home). Notice that because and so are opposites: because + reason; so + result.</p>\n<p>Punctuation: we usually put a comma before but and so when they join two full sentences (It was late, so we went home). We usually do NOT put a comma before because. A group of words that starts with because cannot stand alone as a sentence: 'Because I was tired.' is not complete. In STEP, transition items give you a sentence with a blank and four connectors; read both sides of the blank to see the relationship.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>and</strong> My father is a doctor, and my mother is a teacher. (two similar facts)</p>\n<p><strong>but</strong> The test was long, but it was easy. (contrast)</p>\n<p><strong>or</strong> We can watch a film or play a game. (choice)</p>\n<p><strong>because</strong> Huda was happy because she won the race. (reason)</p>\n<p><strong>so</strong> Huda won the race, so she was happy. (result)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> I was tired, because I went to bed early. → I was tired, so I went to bed early. (result, not reason)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> I like fish but I like chicken. → I like fish and chicken. (similar ideas need and)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Because it was raining. → We stayed inside because it was raining. (a full sentence is needed)</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">أدوات الربط تجمع فكرتين في جملة واحدة: and للإضافة، وbut للتضاد، وor للاختيار، وbecause للسبب (تجيب عن لماذا؟)، وso للنتيجة. وتذكّر أن because وso متعاكستان: because يأتي بعدها السبب وso يأتي بعدها النتيجة. ونضع فاصلة عادةً قبل but وso عندما تربطان جملتين كاملتين، ولا نضعها قبل because.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Read the words before AND after the blank.</p>\n<p>2. Ask: Is the second idea similar (and), different (but), a choice (or), a reason (because) or a result (so)?</p>\n<p>3. Test your answer by asking Why? — if the second part answers Why?, use because.</p>\n<p>4. Read the full sentence with your answer to check that it makes sense.</p>\n<p>5. In error items, check that the connector matches the meaning.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ ما قبل الفراغ وما بعده، واسأل: هل الفكرة الثانية مشابهة أم مختلفة أم اختيار أم سبب أم نتيجة؟ واختبر because بسؤال لماذا؟ ثم اقرأ الجملة كاملة للتأكد من معناها.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ Using because for a result and so for a reason.</p>\n<p>✗ Using and when the ideas are different (contrast needs but).</p>\n<p>✗ Using or in a statement that is not a choice.</p>\n<p>✗ A sentence that starts with Because and stops without a main idea.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which word or phrase best fills the blank?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I was hungry, ______ I made a sandwich.</p>\n<p>A. so B. but C. or D. because</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> First idea: I was hungry. Second idea: I made a sandwich.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The second idea is a result of the first.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A result needs so.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفكرة الثانية نتيجة للأولى، فالصحيح so.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. We wanted to go (A) <u>to</u> the beach, (B) <u>so</u> it (C) <u>was</u> too (D) <u>windy</u>.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. to B. so C. was D. windy</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> We wanted to go, and it was too windy: these ideas are opposite.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> so shows a result, which does not fit here.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B: it should be but.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الخطأ في B لأن المعنى تضاد يحتاج but.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which word or phrase best fills the blank?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I like summer ______ I can swim every day.</p>\n<p>A. but B. because C. or D. so</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Ask: Why do I like summer?</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is after the blank: I can swim every day.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A reason needs because.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجزء الثاني يجيب عن لماذا؟ فالصحيح because.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-A1-03 — My favourite food (with and, but, because)</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write about your favourite food in 40–60 words. Use and, but and because at least once each.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب عن طعامك المفضل في أربعين إلى ستين كلمة، واستخدم and وbut وbecause مرة واحدة على الأقل لكل منها.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Sentence 1: What is your favourite food?</p>\n<p>2. Sentence 2: What is in it? (… and …)</p>\n<p>3. Sentence 3: Who cooks it, and when? (… because …)</p>\n<p>4. Sentence 4: What do you eat it with? What don't you like with it? (… but …)</p>\n<p>5. Sentence 5: Why is it special for you?</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (47 words; target 40–60)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My favourite food is kabsa. It is rice with chicken, and it has a lot of spices. My mother cooks it every Friday because the whole family visits us. I like kabsa with salad, but I don't like it with hot sauce. It is delicious and healthy.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ and joins two similar facts about the food.</p>\n<p>▸ because gives the reason why kabsa is cooked on Friday.</p>\n<p>▸ but shows a contrast between salad and hot sauce, with a comma before it.</p>\n<p>▸ The last sentence repeats the main idea in a new way.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Did I use and, but and because correctly?</p>\n<p>☐ Does because come before a reason?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I put a comma before but and so?</p>\n<p>☐ Is every sentence complete (subject + verb)?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I check capital letters and full stops?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من استخدام and للإضافة وbut للتضاد وbecause للسبب، ومن وضع فاصلة قبل but وso.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 A · Example 2 B · Example 3 B","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["but","or","and","because"],"x":["My sister is clever ______ kind."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] and — Two similar good qualities are joined with and.","h":"صفتان متشابهتان نربطهما بـ and."},{"n":2,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["and","but","or","so"],"x":["I want to play outside, ______ it is raining."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] but — Wanting to play and the rain are a contrast.","h":"تضاد يحتاج but."},{"n":3,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["and","so","or","because"],"x":["Would you like juice ______ water?"],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] or — The question offers a choice.","h":"الاختيار يحتاج or."},{"n":4,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["but","or","because","so"],"x":["We went to the restaurant ______ we were hungry."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] because — Being hungry is the reason for going.","h":"السبب يحتاج because."},{"n":5,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["because","or","but","so"],"x":["The shop was closed, ______ we went home."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] so — Going home is the result of the closed shop.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج so."},{"n":6,"s":"I (A) like cats, (B) because I (C) don't like (D) dogs.","o":["like","because","don't","dogs"],"k":1,"e":"[error] because — Liking cats and not liking dogs is a contrast: but.","h":"التضاد يحتاج but."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence correctly joins these two ideas: 'It was late.' + 'I went to bed.'?","o":["It was late, but I went to bed.","It was late, so I went to bed.","It was late, or I went to bed.","It was late because I went to bed."],"k":1,"e":"[error] It was late, so I went to bed. — Going to bed is the result of being late: so.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج so."},{"n":8,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["but","so","because","or"],"x":["My brother can swim, ______ he can't ride a bike."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] but — can / can't is a contrast.","h":"تضاد يحتاج but."},{"n":9,"s":"We (A) were tired, (B) so we (C) stopped (D) or had a rest.","o":["were","so","stopped","or"],"k":3,"e":"[error] or — stopped and had a rest are two actions together: and.","h":"فعلان معًا يحتاجان and."},{"n":10,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["and","or","because","so"],"x":["Hurry up, ______ you will miss the bus!"],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] or — or here means 'if not': hurry, or you will miss it.","h":"or بمعنى وإلا."},{"n":11,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["but","or","because","so"],"x":["Faisal studied hard, ______ he passed the test."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] so — Passing is the result of studying.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج so."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence uses because correctly?","o":["I am thirsty because I drink water.","Because I drink water. I am thirsty.","I drink water because thirsty.","I drink water because I am thirsty."],"k":3,"e":"[error] I drink water because I am thirsty. — because is followed by the reason (I am thirsty), with a subject and a verb.","h":"بعد because يأتي السبب في جملة كاملة."},{"n":13,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["and","or","so","because"],"x":["I like milk ______ cheese, but I don't like yoghurt."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] and — milk and cheese are two things the speaker likes.","h":"شيئان متشابهان يحتاجان and."},{"n":14,"s":"She (A) was happy (B) because she (C) got a good mark, (D) but she smiled all day.","o":["was","because","got","but"],"k":3,"e":"[error] but — Smiling all day is a result, not a contrast: so.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج so لا but."},{"n":15,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so","but","or","because"],"x":["Our car is old, ______ it still works well."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] but — old / works well is a surprise: but.","h":"المفارقة تحتاج but."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["So I bought two books.","So I borrowed one from the library.","Because I like books.","Or I read a book."],"x":["I wanted to buy a new book, but I didn't have enough money. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] So I borrowed one from the library. — Borrowing is a logical result of not having money.","h":"الاستعارة نتيجة منطقية لعدم وجود المال."},{"n":17,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["or","but","so","because"],"x":["Should we walk ______ take a taxi?"],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] or — The question gives two choices.","h":"خياران يحتاجان or."},{"n":18,"s":"(A) It was (B) hot, (C) or we (D) turned on the air conditioner.","o":["It","hot","or","turned on"],"k":2,"e":"[error] or — Turning on the air conditioner is a result: so.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج so."},{"n":19,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["because","so","or","and"],"x":["I couldn't sleep ______ the room was very noisy."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] because — The noisy room is the reason.","h":"السبب يحتاج because."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["We visited the museum, and we took many photos.","We visited the museum, or we took many photos.","We visited the museum, because we took many photos.","We visited the museum but, we took many photos."],"k":0,"e":"[error] We visited the museum, and we took many photos. — Two actions in the same visit are joined with and.","h":"حدثان متتابعان يربطهما and."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) My favourite food is kabsa. (2) It is rice with chicken or meat. (3) My mother cooks it every Friday. (4) My brother is a good student. (5) I eat it with salad and yoghurt."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The paragraph is about kabsa; the brother's studies are off the topic.","h":"الجملة عن الأخ لا عن الكبسة."},{"n":22,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1"],"x":["(1) After that, he had lunch with his family.","(2) Ali came home from school.","(3) Finally, he did his homework.","(4) Then he washed his hands."],"k":1,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — came home → Then washed → After that, lunch → Finally, homework.","h":"رتّب حسب كلمات التسلسل."},{"n":23,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Lions eat meat.","Africa is a big continent.","Giraffes are amazing animals.","Trees need water."],"x":["______ They are tall and have long necks. They eat leaves from high trees. You can see them in Africa."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Giraffes are amazing animals. — All the details describe giraffes.","h":"التفاصيل كلها عن الزرافة."},{"n":24,"s":"My (A) friends (B) is waiting (C) for me (D) outside.","o":["friends","is","for","outside"],"k":1,"e":"[error] is — friends is plural: are waiting.","h":"الجمع يحتاج are."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My father buys newspapers.","Computers are expensive.","The library is a great place for students.","The break is twenty minutes."],"x":["Our school has a big library. It has thousands of books. Students can read there during the break. There are also computers for research. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] The library is a great place for students. — The conclusion sums up why the library is good.","h":"الخاتمة تلخص الفكرة."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["My friend's birthday is next week.","I need a new watch.","I don't like cake.","My family had a small party for me."],"x":["Yesterday was my birthday. ______ They gave me a new watch. We ate cake and played games."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] My family had a small party for me. — They in the next sentence needs a group of people: my family.","h":"They تحتاج مرجعًا قبلها."},{"n":27,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so","or","but","because"],"x":["Sami is tall, ______ his brother is short."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] but — tall / short is a contrast.","h":"تضاد يحتاج but."},{"n":28,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Taif is a city in the mountains. (2) It is famous for its roses. (3) In summer, the weather is cool. (4) Many families visit it on holiday. (5) My cousin is learning to drive."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — The paragraph is about Taif; the cousin's driving is off the topic.","h":"الجملة الأخيرة خارج الموضوع."},{"n":29,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 1 – 3","2 – 1 – 4 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1"],"x":["(1) my homework","(2) I","(3) after dinner","(4) do"],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — I do my homework after dinner.","h":"فاعل ثم فعل ثم مفعول ثم زمن."},{"n":30,"s":"There (A) is (B) three (C) big windows in (D) our classroom.","o":["is","three","big","our"],"k":0,"e":"[error] is — three windows is plural: There are.","h":"الجمع يحتاج there are."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.4","t":"Basic Punctuation: Comma, Question Mark, Apostrophe","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.4 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Use commas in lists, question marks and apostrophes correctly.</p>\n<p>2. Find punctuation errors in short sentences.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يستخدم الطالب الفاصلة في القوائم وعلامة الاستفهام والفاصلة العليا استخدامًا صحيحًا.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يكتشف أخطاء الترقيم في الجمل القصيرة.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>COMMAS separate things in a list: I bought rice, chicken, tomatoes and onions. We usually put a comma after a short opening phrase (On Friday, we visit our grandparents), after yes / no (Yes, I can), before the name of the person we speak to (Thank you, Sara) and before but and so when they join two sentences.</p>\n<p>A QUESTION MARK (?) ends every direct question: Where do you live? Can you help me? A FULL STOP ends a statement or a polite request that is not a question. Do not use a question mark after a statement (I live in Taif?) or a full stop after a question.</p>\n<p>The APOSTROPHE (’) has two jobs. First, it shows that something belongs to someone: Sara's bag, my father's car, the teacher's desk. Second, it shows that letters are missing in a short form: don't (do not), can't (cannot), it's (it is), I'm (I am). Do NOT use an apostrophe to make a plural: two apples (not apple's). Be careful with its and it's: it's = it is; its = belonging to it (The cat ate its food). Also your (belonging to you) and you're (you are).</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>list</strong> We need bread, eggs, milk and cheese.</p>\n<p><strong>opening</strong> After school, I play football.</p>\n<p><strong>?</strong> Do you like English? · What time is it?</p>\n<p><strong>’s</strong> This is Faisal's bike. · My sister's room is big.</p>\n<p><strong>short form</strong> I don't know. · She can't come. · It's late.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> I have three brother's. → I have three brothers. (plural: no apostrophe)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Its a nice day. → It's a nice day. (it's = it is)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Where is the library. → Where is the library? (question mark)</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفاصلة تفصل بين عناصر القائمة، وتأتي بعد عبارة افتتاحية قصيرة وبعد yes / no وقبل اسم المخاطَب وقبل but وso عند ربط جملتين. وعلامة الاستفهام تنهي كل سؤال مباشر. والفاصلة العليا تدل على الملكية (Sara's bag) أو على حذف حروف (don't, it's)، ولا تُستخدم للجمع (apples لا apple's). وفرّق بين it's بمعنى it is وits بمعنى خاصته، وبين your وyou're.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Check the end of every sentence: question → ?, statement → full stop.</p>\n<p>2. Count the items in a list: put commas between them and and before the last one.</p>\n<p>3. For every word with 's, ask: Is it belonging (Sara's), a short form (it's) or just a plural (books)?</p>\n<p>4. Test it's by reading it is; test you're by reading you are.</p>\n<p>5. Look for a missing apostrophe in short forms: dont, cant, Im, whats.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تحقق من نهاية كل جملة، وضع فواصل بين عناصر القائمة، واسأل عند كل 's: هل هي ملكية أم اختصار أم جمع؟ واختبر it's بقراءتها it is، وابحث عن الفاصلة العليا الناقصة في dont وcant.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ An apostrophe in a plural noun (banana's, car's).</p>\n<p>✗ its and it's, your and you're mixed up.</p>\n<p>✗ A full stop at the end of a question.</p>\n<p>✗ Commas in the wrong place in a list (red, green, and, blue).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. This is (A) <u>my</u> (B) <u>fathers</u> (C) <u>new</u> (D) <u>office</u>.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. my B. fathers C. new D. office</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Look at every word ending in s.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> fathers here means the office of my father, so it shows belonging.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B: father's.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">fathers هنا تعني مكتب أبي، فتحتاج الفاصلة العليا.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which sentence uses commas correctly?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. We need bread eggs and milk. B. We need bread, eggs and milk.</p>\n<p>C. We need, bread, eggs and milk. D. We need bread, eggs, and, milk.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Find the list: bread, eggs, milk.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Put a comma between the first items and and before the last.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> No comma after need or after and.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفاصلة بين عناصر القائمة فقط.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. (A) <u>Where</u> (B) <u>do</u> you (C) <u>live</u> (D) <u>now.</u></strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Where B. do C. live D. now.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The sentence starts with Where do you …: it is a question.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A question must end with a question mark.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is D: now?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة سؤال فيجب أن تنتهي بعلامة استفهام.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-A1-04 — A short note inviting a classmate to my house</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write a short note (40–60 words) inviting a classmate to your house. Use at least one question, one list with commas and two apostrophes.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب رسالة قصيرة (من أربعين إلى ستين كلمة) تدعو فيها زميلًا إلى بيتك، واستخدم سؤالًا واحدًا على الأقل وقائمة بفواصل وفاصلتين عُلويتين.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Greeting: Dear …,</p>\n<p>2. Invitation question: Would you like to come …?</p>\n<p>3. Day and time.</p>\n<p>4. What you will do (a list with commas).</p>\n<p>5. Where you live / how to come.</p>\n<p>6. Closing: Your friend, …</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (54 words; target 40–60)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Dear Yousef, Would you like to come to my house on Thursday? My mother is making pizza, salad and juice for us. We can play my brother's new football game in the garden. Please come at five o'clock. Our house is next to Al-Huda Mosque. Can you tell me by Tuesday? Your friend, Omar</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The note opens and closes with a comma after Dear Yousef and Your friend.</p>\n<p>▸ Two questions end with question marks.</p>\n<p>▸ The list pizza, salad and juice has a comma between the first two items.</p>\n<p>▸ brother's shows belonging with an apostrophe.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Does every question end with a question mark?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I use commas in my list?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I use 's only for belonging or short forms, not for plurals?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I write the day, time and place clearly?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I start and finish the note correctly?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من علامات الاستفهام، والفواصل في القائمة، واستخدام 's للملكية فقط، ومن بداية الرسالة ونهايتها.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 B · Example 3 D","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence is punctuated correctly?","o":["I bought apples bananas and oranges.","I bought apples, bananas and oranges.","I bought, apples, bananas and oranges.","I bought apples, bananas, and, oranges."],"k":1,"e":"[error] I bought apples, bananas and oranges. — Commas separate the items in the list.","h":"الفواصل بين عناصر القائمة."},{"n":2,"s":"(A) Where is my (B) brothers (C) new (D) bike?","o":["Where","brothers","new","bike"],"k":1,"e":"[error] brothers — The bike belongs to my brother: brother's.","h":"الملكية تحتاج 's."},{"n":3,"s":"Which question is punctuated correctly?","o":["Can you help me, please.","Can you help me please!","can you help me, please?","Can you help me, please?"],"k":3,"e":"[error] Can you help me, please? — A question starts with a capital letter and ends with a question mark.","h":"السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"n":4,"s":"My (A) mothers (B) name (C) is (D) Noura.","o":["mothers","name","is","Noura"],"k":0,"e":"[error] mothers — The name belongs to my mother: mother's.","h":"الملكية تحتاج 's."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence uses an apostrophe correctly?","o":["This is Khalids' phone.","This is Khalids phone.","This is Khalid phone's.","This is Khalid's phone."],"k":3,"e":"[error] This is Khalid's phone. — One person (Khalid) owns the phone: Khalid's.","h":"مالك واحد: Khalid's."},{"n":6,"s":"We (A) need (B) egg's, milk (C) and sugar for (D) the cake.","o":["need","egg's","and","the"],"k":1,"e":"[error] egg's — eggs is a plural, not belonging: no apostrophe.","h":"الجمع لا يحتاج فاصلة عليا."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence is punctuated correctly?","o":["On Friday we, visit our grandparents.","On, Friday we visit our grandparents.","On Friday, we visit our grandparents?","On Friday, we visit our grandparents."],"k":3,"e":"[error] On Friday, we visit our grandparents. — A comma follows the opening phrase On Friday; a statement ends with a full stop.","h":"فاصلة بعد العبارة الافتتاحية."},{"n":8,"s":"(A) I'm sorry, but (B) I (C) cant come (D) today.","o":["I'm","I","cant","today"],"k":2,"e":"[error] cant — cannot in short form is can't, with an apostrophe.","h":"الاختصار يحتاج فاصلة عليا: can't."},{"n":9,"s":"Which is a correct question?","o":["How old is your brother?","How old is your brother.","How old your brother is?","how old is your brother?"],"k":0,"e":"[error] How old is your brother? — Correct order, capital letter and question mark.","h":"ترتيب صحيح وحرف كبير وعلامة استفهام."},{"n":10,"s":"(A) Dont (B) forget (C) your bag, (D) Hamad.","o":["Dont","forget","your","Hamad"],"k":0,"e":"[error] Dont — do not in short form is don't.","h":"الاختصار don't."},{"n":11,"s":"Which sentence uses commas correctly?","o":["My favourite colours are red green and blue.","My favourite colours, are red, green and blue.","My favourite colours are red, green and blue.","My favourite, colours are red green, and blue."],"k":2,"e":"[error] My favourite colours are red, green and blue. — Commas go only between the colours.","h":"الفواصل بين الألوان فقط."},{"n":12,"s":"It's (A) cold today, (B) so (C) wear (D) you're coat.","o":["cold","so","wear","you're"],"k":3,"e":"[error] you're — The coat belongs to you: your, not you're (you are).","h":"your للملكية وyou're بمعنى you are."},{"n":13,"s":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["Its raining, so take an umbrella.","It's raining so, take an umbrella.","It's raining, so take an umbrella.","Its' raining, so take an umbrella."],"k":2,"e":"[error] It's raining, so take an umbrella. — It's = it is; the comma comes before so.","h":"It's بمعنى it is والفاصلة قبل so."},{"n":14,"s":"My (A) teachers car (B) is (C) white and (D) very clean.","o":["teachers","is","white","very"],"k":0,"e":"[error] teachers — The car belongs to my teacher: teacher's.","h":"الملكية تحتاج 's."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence needs a question mark at the end?","o":["I live near the school","My school is near my house","Please come to my school","Do you live near the school"],"k":3,"e":"[error] Do you live near the school — Only Do you live … is a question.","h":"السؤال وحده يحتاج علامة استفهام."},{"n":16,"s":"Ahmed, (A) can (B) you pass (C) me the (D) salt.","o":["can","you","me","salt."],"k":3,"e":"[error] salt. — Can you … is a question, so it ends with a question mark.","h":"السؤال ينتهي بعلامة استفهام."},{"n":17,"s":"Which sentence uses an apostrophe correctly?","o":["My sister's room is next to mine.","My sisters room is next to mine.","My sister's room's is next to mine.","My sister room's is next to mine."],"k":0,"e":"[error] My sister's room is next to mine. — The room belongs to my sister: sister's room.","h":"الملكية: sister's room."},{"n":18,"s":"I (A) have two (B) brother's and (C) one (D) sister.","o":["have","brother's","one","sister"],"k":1,"e":"[error] brother's — brothers is a simple plural: no apostrophe.","h":"الجمع بلا فاصلة عليا."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence is punctuated correctly?","o":["Yes, I would like some tea.","Yes I, would like some tea.","Yes, I would like some tea?","Yes I would, like some tea."],"k":0,"e":"[error] Yes, I would like some tea. — A comma follows Yes; a statement ends with a full stop.","h":"فاصلة بعد Yes."},{"n":20,"s":"(A) Whats the (B) name (C) of your (D) school?","o":["Whats","name","of","school"],"k":0,"e":"[error] Whats — what is in short form is what's.","h":"الاختصار what's."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so","or","but","because"],"x":["I called my friend, ______ he didn't answer."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] but — Calling and not answering is a contrast.","h":"التضاد يحتاج but."},{"n":22,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Our classroom is on the first floor. (2) It has twenty desks. (3) There is a big whiteboard at the front. (4) Elephants are very big animals. (5) The walls are light blue. (6) We keep it clean every day."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — Every sentence describes the classroom except the one about elephants.","h":"الجملة عن الفيلة خارج الموضوع."},{"n":23,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["1 – 2 – 4 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","2 – 1 – 4 – 3","2 – 1 – 3 – 4"],"x":["(1) She opened the door and said hello.","(2) Someone knocked on the door.","(3) Then she invited her friend inside.","(4) It was her friend, Mona."],"k":2,"e":"[best order] 2 – 1 – 4 – 3 — knocked → opened → it was Mona → invited inside.","h":"رتّب الأحداث منطقيًا."},{"n":24,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["I don't like cooking.","My house has three rooms.","I like the small café on our street.","Workers need a holiday."],"x":["______ First, it is close to my house. Second, the food is cheap. Third, the workers are very friendly."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] I like the small café on our street. — The reasons (close, cheap, friendly) describe a place the writer likes.","h":"الأسباب تصف مكانًا يحبه الكاتب."},{"n":25,"s":"My little brother (A) don't (B) like (C) vegetables (D) at all.","o":["don't","like","vegetables","at all"],"k":0,"e":"[error] don't — My little brother is singular: doesn't.","h":"الفاعل مفرد فنستخدم doesn't."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Dogs are good pets.","I love my cat very much.","My bed is very big.","I bought a new ball."],"x":["My cat, Lulu, is three years old. She is white with grey ears. She sleeps on my bed every night. She plays with a small ball. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] I love my cat very much. — The conclusion returns to the main topic, the cat.","h":"الخاتمة تعود إلى القطة."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["The zoo opens at nine.","We saw lions and monkeys.","I don't like hot weather.","My father works on Saturday."],"x":["Last Saturday, we went to the zoo. ______ We also saw a big elephant. It was a fun day."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] We saw lions and monkeys. — 'We also saw' needs another seeing sentence before it.","h":"also تحتاج جملة رؤية قبلها."},{"n":28,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["and","so","but","or"],"x":["I can't find my keys. Did you take them, ______ are they in the car?"],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] or — The question offers two possibilities.","h":"احتمالان يحتاجان or."},{"n":29,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 2 – 1 – 4","1 – 3 – 2 – 4","3 – 1 – 2 – 4","3 – 1 – 4 – 2"],"x":["(1) wrote","(2) a letter","(3) My brother","(4) to our grandmother"],"k":2,"e":"[best order] 3 – 1 – 2 – 4 — My brother wrote a letter to our grandmother.","h":"فاعل ثم فعل ثم مفعول ثم إلى من."},{"n":30,"s":"Yesterday (A) we (B) eat (C) lunch at (D) a restaurant.","o":["we","eat","lunch","a"],"k":1,"e":"[error] eat — Yesterday needs the past tense: ate.","h":"الماضي ate."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.5","t":"Writing about Myself and My Family (Guided Paragraph)","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.5 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Write a guided paragraph of 40–60 words about myself and my family.</p>\n<p>2. Recognize a simple opening and closing sentence.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يكتب الطالب فقرة موجهة من أربعين إلى ستين كلمة عن نفسه وعن أسرته.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يتعرف على جملة افتتاحية وجملة ختامية بسيطتين.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>A paragraph is a group of sentences about ONE topic. A good paragraph has three parts. The OPENING sentence (also called the topic sentence) tells the reader what the paragraph is about: I have a small family. The MIDDLE sentences give details: names, ages, jobs, likes. The CLOSING sentence (the concluding sentence) ends the paragraph and repeats the main idea in new words: I love my small family very much.</p>\n<p>A good opening sentence is general: it covers ALL the details that come after it. 'My father is an engineer' is too narrow to open a paragraph about the whole family; 'There are five people in my family' is better. A good closing sentence is connected to the topic and often shows a feeling or opinion: That is why I am proud of my family.</p>\n<p>In STEP, topic-sentence items show a paragraph with a blank at the beginning; concluding-sentence items show a blank at the end. Wrong options are usually (1) too narrow — only one detail, (2) off the topic, or (3) about a new idea that the paragraph does not discuss.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>opening</strong> There are five people in my family. (general: covers all the details)</p>\n<p><strong>details</strong> My father is a pilot. My mother is a nurse. I have two brothers.</p>\n<p><strong>closing</strong> We are a busy family, but we always find time to be together.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ too narrow</strong> My father likes coffee. (only one detail, cannot open the paragraph)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ off topic</strong> Riyadh has many tall buildings. (not about the family)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ new idea</strong> Next year, I want to buy a new bike. (a new idea at the end)</p>\n<p><strong>opening</strong> My grandmother is the most special person in my life.</p>\n<p><strong>closing</strong> I hope I can be as kind as my grandmother one day.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفقرة مجموعة جمل عن موضوع واحد، ولها ثلاثة أجزاء: الجملة الافتتاحية (جملة الموضوع) التي تخبر القارئ بموضوع الفقرة، والجمل الداعمة التي تعطي التفاصيل، والجملة الختامية التي تنهي الفقرة وتعيد الفكرة الرئيسة بكلمات جديدة. والجملة الافتتاحية الجيدة عامة تشمل كل التفاصيل، والبدائل الخاطئة عادةً ضيقة جدًا أو خارج الموضوع أو تأتي بفكرة جديدة.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Read all the sentences first and ask: What is this paragraph about?</p>\n<p>2. For an opening sentence, choose the option that covers ALL the details.</p>\n<p>3. For a closing sentence, choose the option that repeats the main idea or gives a feeling about it.</p>\n<p>4. Reject options that give only one small detail.</p>\n<p>5. Reject options about a different topic or a new idea.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ الجمل كلها واسأل: عمّ تتحدث الفقرة؟ واختر للافتتاح الجملة التي تشمل كل التفاصيل، وللختام الجملة التي تعيد الفكرة الرئيسة أو تعبر عن شعور تجاهها، وارفض الجمل الضيقة أو الخارجة عن الموضوع.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ A detail sentence offered as the opening sentence.</p>\n<p>✗ A sentence that uses a word from the paragraph but talks about something else.</p>\n<p>✗ A closing sentence that starts a new topic.</p>\n<p>✗ A true sentence that does not fit this paragraph.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>______ My father is a pilot, and my mother is a doctor. I have one sister. Her name is Rana.</p>\n<p>A. My father flies to London. B. I have a small family.</p>\n<p>C. Doctors help sick people. D. Rana is a beautiful name.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Read the details: father, mother, sister.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The paragraph is about the whole family.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'I have a small family' covers all the details; the other options are one detail or off the topic.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة الافتتاحية يجب أن تشمل أفراد الأسرة جميعًا.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My best friend is Saud. He is funny and kind. We sit together in class. We play football after school. ______</p>\n<p>A. Football is my favourite sport.</p>\n<p>B. Our class has thirty students.</p>\n<p>C. Saud has a brother.</p>\n<p>D. I am lucky to have a friend like Saud.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Main idea: Saud is my best friend.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A good closing sentence repeats this idea or gives a feeling about it.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'I am lucky to have a friend like Saud' does both.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الخاتمة تعيد فكرة الصداقة مع التعبير عن شعور.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>(1)</strong> My family loves camping. <strong>(2)</strong> We go to the desert in winter. <strong>(3)</strong> We sleep in a big tent. <strong>(4)</strong> My school starts at seven. <strong>(5)</strong> At night, we look at the stars.</p>\n<p>A. Sentence 2 B. Sentence 3 C. Sentence 4 D. Sentence 5</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Topic: my family's camping trips.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Check each sentence: desert, tent, stars are about camping.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Sentence 4 about school does not belong.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة الرابعة لا علاقة لها بالتخييم.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-A1-05 — Myself and my family</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write a paragraph of 40–60 words about yourself and your family. Start with an opening sentence and finish with a closing sentence.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب فقرة من أربعين إلى ستين كلمة عن نفسك وعن أسرتك، وابدأها بجملة افتتاحية واختمها بجملة ختامية.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Opening sentence: Who are you? (name, age, city)</p>\n<p>2. Detail: Who is in your family?</p>\n<p>3. Detail: What are their jobs or what do they like?</p>\n<p>4. Detail: What do you do together?</p>\n<p>5. Closing sentence: How do you feel about your family?</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (52 words; target 40–60)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My name is Faris, and I am eleven years old. I live in Taif with my family. My father is an engineer, and my mother is a teacher. I have one brother and two sisters. We eat dinner together every evening and talk about our day. I love my family very much.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The opening sentence introduces the writer.</p>\n<p>▸ The middle sentences give clear details about the family and what they do together.</p>\n<p>▸ The closing sentence shows a feeling about the family and ends the paragraph well.</p>\n<p>▸ and joins ideas, and every sentence is complete.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Does my first sentence introduce me?</p>\n<p>☐ Do all my middle sentences talk about my family?</p>\n<p>☐ Does my last sentence show a feeling or repeat the main idea?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my paragraph 40–60 words?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I check capital letters, full stops and is / are?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من أن الجملة الأولى تعرّف بك، وأن جمل الوسط عن أسرتك، وأن الجملة الأخيرة تعبر عن شعورك أو تعيد الفكرة الرئيسة.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 D · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["There are six people in my family.","My father likes coffee.","Teachers work very hard.","I go to school by bus."],"x":["______ My father is an engineer. My mother is a teacher. I have one brother and two sisters."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] There are six people in my family. — The details describe all six family members.","h":"التفاصيل عن الأسرة كلها."},{"n":2,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My cousin lives in Riyadh.","Swimming pools are expensive.","Jeddah has a big airport.","I am a happy boy, and I love my city."],"x":["My name is Majed. I am ten years old. I live in Jeddah with my family. I like reading and swimming. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence] I am a happy boy, and I love my city. — The closing sentence returns to the writer with a feeling.","h":"الخاتمة تعود إلى الكاتب مع شعور."},{"n":3,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Cookies are sweet.","My grandmother is very special to me.","I read a story yesterday.","My grandfather has a farm."],"x":["______ She is sixty-five years old. She tells us stories every night. She makes the best date cookies."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] My grandmother is very special to me. — All the details are about the grandmother.","h":"التفاصيل عن الجدة."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Basketball is a fast game.","He is a great brother.","My homework is easy.","The school team has ten players."],"x":["My brother Ziyad is twelve. He is tall and strong. He plays basketball for the school team. He also helps me with my homework. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] He is a great brother. — The closing sentence sums up the paragraph about Ziyad.","h":"الخاتمة تلخص الفقرة عن زياد."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Our dining table is brown.","I don't like dinner.","My friend eats at a restaurant.","My family likes to spend time together."],"x":["______ We have a big dining room. We eat together every evening. We talk about our day."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] My family likes to spend time together. — The details show the family together; the opening must cover this idea.","h":"الفكرة: الأسرة تقضي الوقت معًا."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["I think she will be a great artist one day.","Our kitchen is small.","I like colouring books.","Artists live in big cities."],"x":["My sister Lama is eight years old. She likes drawing and colouring. Her pictures are on our kitchen wall. She wants to be an artist. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] I think she will be a great artist one day. — The closing sentence connects to her dream and gives an opinion.","h":"الخاتمة ترتبط بحلمها وتعبر عن رأي."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) My name is Turki. (2) I am eleven years old. (3) I live in Dammam with my parents. (4) The Red Sea is very beautiful. (5) I have two younger brothers."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The paragraph introduces Turki; the Red Sea is off the topic.","h":"الجملة عن البحر الأحمر خارج الموضوع."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Mint is good in tea.","My grandfather loves his garden.","My uncle has a new car.","Tomatoes are red."],"x":["______ Every morning, he waters the plants. In the afternoon, he reads in the garden. He grows tomatoes and mint."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] My grandfather loves his garden. — All the details are about the grandfather and his garden.","h":"التفاصيل عن الجد وحديقته."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Our school is very old.","Football is popular in Brazil.","Nasser is my cousin and my best friend.","I have many books."],"x":["I have a cousin called Nasser. He lives near our house. We go to the same school. We play football together every weekend. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] Nasser is my cousin and my best friend. — The closing sentence repeats the main idea about Nasser.","h":"الخاتمة تعيد الفكرة عن ناصر."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Newspapers are not expensive.","Everyone in my family is busy on Saturday morning.","My room is very big.","I don't like cleaning."],"x":["______ My father reads the newspaper. My mother cooks lunch. My sisters and I clean our rooms."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Everyone in my family is busy on Saturday morning. — The opening covers what every family member does.","h":"الافتتاح يشمل ما يفعله كل فرد."},{"n":11,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Hospitals are very busy.","My father works in a bank.","I was sick last week.","I am very proud of my mother."],"x":["My mother is a nurse. She works at a big hospital. She helps sick people every day. She is kind and patient. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence] I am very proud of my mother. — The closing sentence shows a feeling about the mother.","h":"الخاتمة تعبر عن شعور تجاه الأم."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Parrots are colourful birds.","Let me tell you about my friend Bader.","Pilots fly planes.","Makkah is a holy city."],"x":["______ He was born in Makkah. He has a pet parrot. He wants to be a pilot."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Let me tell you about my friend Bader. — The details describe one person, so the opening introduces him.","h":"الافتتاح يعرّف بالشخص."},{"n":13,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) We have a small family. (2) There are only three of us: my father, my mother and me. (3) We live in a flat in Riyadh. (4) Lions live in Africa. (5) We are a small but happy family."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The sentence about lions has nothing to do with the family.","h":"الجملة عن الأسود خارج الموضوع."},{"n":14,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Lamb is expensive.","My grandparents have a cat.","Friday is the best day of the week for my family.","The yard is next to the street."],"x":["Every Friday, my family visits my grandparents. We have lunch together. My grandmother cooks rice and lamb. After lunch, the children play in the yard. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] Friday is the best day of the week for my family. — The closing sentence returns to Friday visits with an opinion.","h":"الخاتمة تعود إلى يوم الجمعة."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My father is a good swimmer.","Animals live in the forest.","Stories are long.","I have many hobbies."],"x":["______ I like reading stories. I also like drawing animals. On Saturdays, I swim with my father."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] I have many hobbies. — Reading, drawing and swimming are all hobbies.","h":"القراءة والرسم والسباحة هوايات."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Japan is in Asia.","Toy planes are cheap.","I want to be a pilot like my uncle.","My aunt doesn't travel."],"x":["My uncle Saleh is a pilot. He flies to many countries. He brings us gifts from his trips. Last month, he gave me a toy plane from Japan. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] I want to be a pilot like my uncle. — The closing sentence connects the paragraph to the writer's feeling.","h":"الخاتمة تربط الفقرة بشعور الكاتب."},{"n":17,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My baby sister is very cute.","Brown is my favourite colour.","My mother has curly hair.","Babies sleep a lot."],"x":["______ She is two years old. She has big brown eyes and curly hair. She laughs all the time."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] My baby sister is very cute. — All the details describe a two-year-old sister.","h":"التفاصيل عن الأخت الصغيرة."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My father has a white car.","When we all help, our home is clean and happy.","Rubbish is bad for the environment.","I like eating dinner."],"x":["In my family, everyone has a job at home. My father washes the car. My mother plans the meals. My brother takes out the rubbish, and I set the table. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] When we all help, our home is clean and happy. — The closing sentence sums up the idea of sharing jobs.","h":"الخاتمة تلخص فكرة تقاسم الأعمال."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My parents like shopping.","Our relatives live far away.","Eid is a busy and happy time for my family.","Lunch is at two o'clock."],"x":["______ First, my parents buy new clothes for us. Then we visit our relatives. Finally, we eat a big lunch together."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Eid is a busy and happy time for my family. — The steps describe the family's Eid; the opening must name it.","h":"التفاصيل تصف العيد."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Doctors work at night.","I love my family and my home.","Grade 4 is difficult.","Gardens need water."],"x":["I am Hessa, and I am in Grade 4. I have two brothers and one sister. My mother is a teacher, and my father is a doctor. We live in a house with a small garden. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] I love my family and my home. — The closing sentence covers the family and the home with a feeling.","h":"الخاتمة تشمل الأسرة والبيت."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so","but","because","or"],"x":["My father is tired, ______ he is still working."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] but — tired / still working is a contrast.","h":"التضاد يحتاج but."},{"n":22,"s":"My (A) brother (B) and my sister (C) is at (D) school now.","o":["brother","and","is","school"],"k":2,"e":"[error] is — Two people (my brother and my sister) need are.","h":"فاعلان يحتاجان are."},{"n":23,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 1 – 4 – 2","3 – 4 – 1 – 2","1 – 3 – 4 – 2","3 – 1 – 2 – 4"],"x":["(1) We wear our new clothes.","(2) After the prayer, we visit our family.","(3) On Eid morning, we wake up early.","(4) Then we go to the Eid prayer."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 3 – 1 – 4 – 2 — wake up → clothes → Then prayer → After the prayer, visits.","h":"رتّب أحداث صباح العيد."},{"n":24,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) The library is my favourite place at school. (2) It is quiet and bright. (3) There are many interesting books. (4) The football pitch is behind the school. (5) I go there every break."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The paragraph is about the library; the football pitch is a different place.","h":"الجملة عن الملعب خارج الموضوع."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Grey is a dark colour.","My ears are small.","The elephant is a very large animal.","Trees have trunks too."],"x":["______ It is big and grey. It has a long trunk and big ears."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] The elephant is a very large animal. — The details (trunk, big ears) describe an elephant.","h":"التفاصيل تصف الفيل."},{"n":26,"s":"(A) Every day, my (B) grandmother (C) drink two cups (D) of tea.","o":["Every","grandmother","drink","of"],"k":2,"e":"[error] drink — my grandmother is singular: drinks.","h":"الفاعل مفرد فالفعل drinks."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["I asked my parents for a dog.","Dogs eat meat.","My friend has a fish.","Next month is May."],"x":["I want a pet. ______ My mother says a cat is easier. Maybe we will get one next month."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] I asked my parents for a dog. — 'a cat is easier' answers a request for a different pet.","h":"الجملة التالية ترد على طلب كلب."},{"n":28,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["but","so","or","because"],"x":["We can eat at home ______ go to a restaurant."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] or — Two choices are joined with or.","h":"خياران يحتاجان or."},{"n":29,"s":"(A) Hes my (B) best friend, and (C) his name (D) is Rakan.","o":["Hes","best","his","is"],"k":0,"e":"[error] Hes — he is in short form is he's.","h":"الاختصار he's."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["We must not waste water.","Cooking is fun.","Animals live in the zoo.","I drink milk at breakfast."],"x":["Water is very important. We drink it every day. We use it to cook and clean. Plants and animals need it too. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] We must not waste water. — The closing sentence gives advice that follows from the main idea.","h":"الخاتمة نصيحة تنبع من الفكرة الرئيسة."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.6","t":"Which Sentence Does Not Belong? (Simple Relevance)","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.6 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Identify the sentence that does not belong to a short paragraph.</p>\n<p>2. Explain why a sentence is off-topic.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يحدد الطالب الجملة التي لا تنتمي إلى فقرة قصيرة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يشرح سبب خروج الجملة عن الموضوع.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>Every sentence in a paragraph must be about the SAME topic. If a paragraph is about a bicycle, every sentence must tell us something about the bicycle. A sentence about cooking, the weather or a cousin does not belong, even if it is a correct English sentence.</p>\n<p>In STEP, irrelevant-sentence items give a paragraph with numbered sentences, and you choose the number of the sentence that does not belong. First, find the topic: it is usually in sentence 1. Then test each sentence with the question: Does this tell me more about the topic? The sentence that answers NO is the answer.</p>\n<p>Be careful: the wrong sentence often uses a word that looks connected. In a paragraph about the beach, 'My cousin's school has a new swimming pool' mentions swimming, but it is about a school, not the beach. Sentence 1 (the topic sentence) is almost never the answer, and the last sentence is often a concluding sentence that belongs.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>topic</strong> My bicycle is my favourite thing.</p>\n<p><strong>✓ belongs</strong> I ride it to school every day. (tells us more about the bicycle)</p>\n<p><strong>✓ belongs</strong> It is red and has a small bell.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ off topic</strong> My mother likes cooking. (a different topic)</p>\n<p><strong>topic</strong> Our school has a big library.</p>\n<p><strong>✓ belongs</strong> It has thousands of books and ten computers.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ tricky</strong> My father reads many books at home. (books, but not about the school library)</p>\n<p><strong>✓ closing</strong> The library is the best place in our school.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">يجب أن تكون كل جمل الفقرة عن موضوع واحد، والجملة التي تتحدث عن شيء آخر لا تنتمي إليها حتى لو كانت صحيحة لغويًا. ابحث عن الموضوع في الجملة الأولى عادةً، ثم اختبر كل جملة بسؤال: هل تخبرني بشيء جديد عن الموضوع؟ واحذر من الجملة التي تحتوي على كلمة تبدو مرتبطة لكنها عن موضوع آخر.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Read sentence 1 and write the topic in two or three words.</p>\n<p>2. Test each sentence: Does it tell me more about the topic?</p>\n<p>3. Watch for sentences that share a word with the topic but talk about something else.</p>\n<p>4. Remember that the first sentence is the topic and the last is often a closing sentence.</p>\n<p>5. Read the paragraph again without your answer: it should flow better.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ الجملة الأولى واكتب الموضوع في كلمتين أو ثلاث، واختبر كل جملة: هل تضيف شيئًا عن الموضوع؟ واحذر من الجمل التي تشترك في كلمة مع الموضوع لكنها عن شيء آخر، ثم اقرأ الفقرة دون الجملة التي اخترتها.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ Choosing a sentence that adds a new but relevant detail.</p>\n<p>✗ Choosing the closing sentence because it sounds different.</p>\n<p>✗ Missing an off-topic sentence that repeats a word from the topic.</p>\n<p>✗ Choosing sentence 1 (the topic sentence).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>(1)</strong> Our school garden is beautiful. <strong>(2)</strong> It has many flowers. <strong>(3)</strong> My father is a police officer. <strong>(4)</strong> There are tall palm trees. <strong>(5)</strong> Students sit there in the break.</p>\n<p>A. Sentence 2 B. Sentence 3 C. Sentence 4 D. Sentence 5</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Topic: our school garden.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Flowers, palm trees and students in the break are all about the garden.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Sentence 3 about the father does not belong.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة الثالثة لا تتحدث عن الحديقة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>(1)</strong> Cats are popular pets. <strong>(2)</strong> They are soft and clean. <strong>(3)</strong> They like to sleep a lot. <strong>(4)</strong> They play with balls and toys. <strong>(5)</strong> The Nile is a long river. <strong>(6)</strong> Many children want a cat at home.</p>\n<p>A. Sentence 3 B. Sentence 4 C. Sentence 5 D. Sentence 6</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Topic: cats as pets.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Sentences 2, 3, 4 and 6 describe cats.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Sentence 5 about the Nile does not belong.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة الخامسة لا علاقة لها بالقطط.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My favourite season is spring. ______ The flowers grow, and the birds sing.</p>\n<p>A. Winter is very cold. B. My birthday is in August.</p>\n<p>C. The weather is warm and sunny. D. I like cold drinks.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Topic: spring, my favourite season.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The sentence after the blank describes spring (flowers, birds).</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only 'The weather is warm and sunny' describes spring.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اختر الجملة التي تبقى في موضوع الربيع.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-A1-06 — My favourite place in my city</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write 40–60 words about your favourite place in your city. Make sure every sentence is about that place.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب من أربعين إلى ستين كلمة عن مكانك المفضل في مدينتك، وتأكد من أن كل جملة تتحدث عن هذا المكان.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Opening sentence: What is your favourite place, and where is it?</p>\n<p>2. Detail: What does it look like?</p>\n<p>3. Detail: What do people do there?</p>\n<p>4. Detail: What do you do there?</p>\n<p>5. Closing sentence: Why is it your favourite place?</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (53 words; target 40–60)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My favourite place in Jeddah is the Corniche. It is a long road next to the Red Sea. In the evening, the air is cool and fresh. Families walk, ride bikes and eat ice cream there. I like to watch the boats and the sunset. The Corniche is the best place to relax.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The opening sentence names the place and the city.</p>\n<p>▸ Every middle sentence describes the Corniche: the road, the air, the people and the writer's activities.</p>\n<p>▸ No sentence talks about another topic.</p>\n<p>▸ The closing sentence gives the reason it is the writer's favourite place.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Is every sentence about my favourite place?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I name the place in the first sentence?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I include what it looks like and what people do there?</p>\n<p>☐ Does my last sentence say why I like it?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I check capital letters for names of places?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ كل جملة واسأل: هل هي عن مكاني المفضل؟ احذف أي جملة خارج الموضوع.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 C · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) My bicycle is red. (2) I ride it to my friend's house. (3) My mother likes cooking. (4) I always wear a helmet. (5) I clean my bicycle every week."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 3 — The paragraph is about the bicycle; cooking is off the topic.","h":"الطبخ خارج موضوع الدراجة."},{"n":2,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Our teacher, Mr. Saad, is very kind. (2) The bus is late today. (3) He explains the lessons clearly. (4) He smiles at us every morning. (5) All the students like him."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 2 — The paragraph describes the teacher; the late bus is off the topic.","h":"تأخر الحافلة خارج موضوع المعلم."},{"n":3,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) The beach is a great place in summer. (2) Children build sandcastles. (3) Families swim in the sea. (4) Some people eat lunch under umbrellas. (5) My cousin's school has a new gym. (6) Everyone has fun at the beach."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — The school gym has nothing to do with the beach.","h":"صالة المدرسة خارج موضوع الشاطئ."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) In winter, we wear warm clothes. (2) My father wears a thick jacket. (3) Mangoes grow in hot countries. (4) My sister wears a wool hat. (5) I wear gloves on cold mornings. (6) Warm clothes keep us healthy."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 3 — Mangoes are off the topic of winter clothes.","h":"المانجو خارج موضوع ملابس الشتاء."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Bees are small but important insects. (2) They make honey. (3) They help flowers to grow. (4) Some bees live in big groups. (5) My uncle has a new car."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — Every sentence is about bees except the uncle's car.","h":"سيارة العم خارج موضوع النحل."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Our school had a sports day last week. (2) My favourite food is pasta. (3) We ran races in the morning. (4) In the afternoon, we played football. (5) The winners got medals. (6) It was an exciting day."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 2 — Pasta has nothing to do with sports day.","h":"المعكرونة خارج موضوع اليوم الرياضي."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) A market is a busy place. (2) People buy fruit and vegetables there. (3) Sellers shout the prices. (4) You can also buy clothes and spices. (5) Many families go there on Thursday. (6) My English book has a blue cover."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 6 — The English book is off the topic of the market.","h":"كتاب الإنجليزي خارج موضوع السوق."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) The moon is our closest neighbour in space. (2) It goes around the Earth. (3) We can see it at night. (4) Tea is a popular drink. (5) It looks different every night."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — Tea has nothing to do with the moon.","h":"الشاي خارج موضوع القمر."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Rain is very important for farmers. (2) It helps plants grow. (3) It fills rivers and lakes. (4) My brother's birthday is in June. (5) Without rain, animals have no water. (6) Everyone is happy when it rains in the desert."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The birthday is off the topic of rain.","h":"عيد الميلاد خارج موضوع المطر."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) Saudi coffee is a famous drink. (2) It is yellow and has cardamom in it. (3) My computer is very slow. (4) People serve it to guests. (5) They usually drink it with dates. (6) It is a sign of welcome."],"k":0,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 3 — The slow computer is off the topic of Saudi coffee.","h":"الحاسوب خارج موضوع القهوة."},{"n":11,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) My friend Sultan lives next door. (2) We walk to school together. (3) He is very good at maths. (4) Penguins cannot fly. (5) He helps me when I have problems. (6) On weekends, we ride our bikes. (7) I am happy that he is my neighbour."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — Penguins have nothing to do with Sultan.","h":"البطاريق خارج موضوع الصديق."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) There is a park near our house. (2) It has swings and slides. (3) My father reads many books. (4) Small children love to play there. (5) We go to the park every evening."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 3 — The father's reading is off the topic of the park.","h":"قراءة الأب خارج موضوع الحديقة."},{"n":13,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) My father bought a new car last month. (2) It is white and very big. (3) It has seven seats. (4) We can all travel in it together. (5) Cats sleep for many hours every day. (6) We love our new car."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — Cats are off the topic of the new car.","h":"القطط خارج موضوع السيارة."},{"n":14,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Ramadan is a special month for Muslims. (2) Winter is cold in the north. (3) People fast from sunrise to sunset. (4) Families eat iftar together. (5) Many people give food to the poor. (6) Everyone feels happy at the end of the month."],"k":0,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 2 — The cold winter is off the topic of Ramadan.","h":"الشتاء خارج موضوع رمضان."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6","Sentence 7"],"x":["(1) Healthy food is important for children. (2) Fruit gives us vitamins. (3) Vegetables keep our bodies strong. (4) Milk is good for our teeth and bones. (5) Water is better than fizzy drinks. (6) My cousin plays the guitar. (7) Eating well helps us learn at school."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 6 — The guitar is off the topic of healthy food.","h":"الجيتار خارج موضوع الطعام الصحي."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Our class has a pet fish. (2) His name is Bubbles. (3) He is orange and white. (4) My sister likes pink shoes. (5) We feed him every morning. (6) Bubbles makes our classroom happy."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — Pink shoes are off the topic of the class fish.","h":"الحذاء الوردي خارج موضوع السمكة."},{"n":17,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["My school is in the city.","The village is quiet and green.","Cars are very fast.","I like video games."],"x":["My grandmother's house is in a small village. ______ There are many trees and a small farm. I love visiting it."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] The village is quiet and green. — The missing sentence must describe the village, like the next sentence.","h":"الجملة الناقصة تصف القرية."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Ships sail on the sea.","Horses are faster than camels.","The desert is very cold at night.","They can also carry heavy things."],"x":["Camels are called 'ships of the desert'. They can walk for many days. ______ That is why people use them to travel in the desert."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] They can also carry heavy things. — The missing sentence gives another reason why camels are useful for travel.","h":"الجملة الناقصة سبب آخر لفائدة الجمل."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) On Saturday, my family has a big breakfast. (2) Lions are strong animals. (3) We eat eggs, cheese and bread. (4) My father makes tea for everyone. (5) We talk and laugh together."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 2 — Lions have nothing to do with the family breakfast.","h":"الأسود خارج موضوع الإفطار."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["First, I feed my little brother.","My mother is a doctor.","My bed is very soft.","I like the weekend."],"x":["Every morning, I help my mother. ______ Then I make my bed and clean my room."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] First, I feed my little brother. — Then needs a first helping action before it.","h":"Then تحتاج خطوة أولى قبلها."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Riyadh is a big, modern city.","My grandfather lives in a village.","Cars are noisy.","I don't like shopping."],"x":["______ It has many tall buildings. The streets are busy with cars. There are big shopping malls."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Riyadh is a big, modern city. — The details describe a big, modern city.","h":"التفاصيل تصف مدينة كبيرة حديثة."},{"n":22,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so","because","or","but"],"x":["We cannot play outside ______ it is very hot."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] because — The heat is the reason we cannot play.","h":"السبب يحتاج because."},{"n":23,"s":"My (A) friends (B) name (C) is (D) Rayan.","o":["friends","name","is","Rayan"],"k":0,"e":"[error] friends — The name belongs to my friend: friend's.","h":"الملكية تحتاج 's."},{"n":24,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1","2 – 4 – 1 – 3"],"x":["(1) Then she added salt and lemon.","(2) First, Noura washed the vegetables.","(3) Finally, she put everything in a bowl.","(4) Next, she cut the vegetables."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — First → Next → Then → Finally.","h":"رتّب حسب كلمات التسلسل."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Everyone in our street loves Mr. Ali.","Shopping is fun on Fridays.","Trees need a lot of water.","Mr. Ali has a blue car."],"x":["Our neighbour, Mr. Ali, is a kind man. He helps old people with their shopping. He waters the trees in our street. He always says hello to the children. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] Everyone in our street loves Mr. Ali. — The closing sentence sums up Mr. Ali's kindness.","h":"الخاتمة تلخص لطف السيد علي."},{"n":26,"s":"We (A) has (B) two English lessons (C) every (D) day.","o":["has","two","every","day"],"k":0,"e":"[error] has — We needs have.","h":"We تحتاج have."},{"n":27,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["but","so","or","because"],"x":["It was my brother's birthday, ______ we bought him a cake."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] so — Buying a cake is the result of the birthday.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج so."},{"n":28,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["My pencil case is blue and green.","I bought new pencils last year.","The library opens at eight.","I looked for it everywhere, but I couldn't find it."],"x":["I lost my pencil case at school. ______ The next day, the teacher found it in the library."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] I looked for it everywhere, but I couldn't find it. — The missing sentence connects losing the case and finding it the next day.","h":"الجملة الناقصة تربط بين الضياع والعثور."},{"n":29,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 2 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 1 – 4","3 – 1 – 2 – 4","1 – 3 – 2 – 4"],"x":["(1) in the mosque","(2) prays","(3) My grandfather","(4) five times a day"],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 3 – 2 – 1 – 4 — My grandfather prays in the mosque five times a day.","h":"فاعل ثم فعل ثم مكان ثم زمن."},{"n":30,"s":"(A) Yesterday it (B) was very hot, so we (C) stay at (D) home.","o":["Yesterday","was","stay","home"],"k":2,"e":"[error] stay — Yesterday needs the past tense: stayed.","h":"الماضي stayed."}]}],"n":30}],"sc":{},"review":{"quiz":[{"l":["Unit Review — 50 questions covering all six lessons of the unit. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","مراجعة الوحدة: خمسون سؤالًا تغطي دروس الوحدة الستة، اختر الإجابة الصحيحة."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["My aunt a dentist.","my aunt is a dentist.","Is a dentist my aunt.","My aunt is a dentist."],"k":3,"e":"[error · 1.1] My aunt is a dentist. — Capital letter, subject (My aunt) and verb (is).","h":"حرف كبير وفاعل وفعل."},{"n":2,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["but","so","and","because"],"x":["I have a pen ______ a pencil in my bag."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector · 1.3] and — Two similar things are joined with and.","h":"شيئان متشابهان يحتاجان and."},{"n":3,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) My grandfather has a farm. (2) He grows dates and lemons. (3) My school bag is heavy. (4) He also has goats and sheep. (5) I visit his farm every holiday."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 1.6] Sentence 3 — The school bag is off the topic of the farm.","h":"الحقيبة خارج موضوع المزرعة."},{"n":4,"s":"(A) Is this (B) Nawafs (C) pencil or (D) yours?","o":["Is","Nawafs","pencil","yours"],"k":1,"e":"[error · 1.4] Nawafs — The pencil belongs to Nawaf: Nawaf's.","h":"الملكية تحتاج 's."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence has the correct word order?","o":["We have a garden small.","Have we a small garden.","We have a small garden.","We a small garden have."],"k":2,"e":"[error · 1.2] We have a small garden. — The adjective small comes before garden.","h":"الصفة قبل الاسم."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Children like toys.","Universities are big.","My father is forty.","My oldest brother is a student."],"x":["______ He is twenty years old. He studies medicine at university. He wants to be a children's doctor."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 1.5] My oldest brother is a student. — The details describe one person, a student, so the opening introduces him.","h":"التفاصيل عن الأخ الطالب."},{"n":7,"s":"(A) My grandparents (B) very (C) old but (D) active.","o":["My","very","old","active"],"k":1,"e":"[error · 1.1] very — The verb are is missing: My grandparents are very old.","h":"ينقص الفعل are."},{"n":8,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["and","because","so","or"],"x":["Close the window, ______ the cat will go outside."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector · 1.3] or — or here means 'if not'.","h":"or بمعنى وإلا."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Our mosque is very beautiful. (2) It has a tall white minaret. (3) There is a green carpet inside. (4) My cousin is a good singer. (5) Many people pray there every day. (6) We are proud of our mosque."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 1.6] Sentence 4 — The cousin's singing is off the topic of the mosque.","h":"الجملة عن ابن العم خارج الموضوع."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence is punctuated correctly?","o":["Thank you Mr, Fahd.","Thank, you Mr. Fahd.","Thank you Mr. Fahd?","Thank you, Mr. Fahd."],"k":3,"e":"[error · 1.4] Thank you, Mr. Fahd. — A comma comes before the name of the person we speak to.","h":"فاصلة قبل اسم المخاطَب."},{"n":11,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 1 – 2 – 4","2 – 3 – 1 – 4","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","3 – 2 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) a big breakfast","(2) eats","(3) My uncle","(4) every day"],"k":3,"e":"[best order · 1.2] 3 – 2 – 1 – 4 — My uncle eats a big breakfast every day.","h":"فاعل ثم فعل ثم مفعول ثم زمن."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["I always enjoy my time with Afnan.","Abha has many mountains.","Painting is a hobby.","Summer is very hot."],"x":["My cousin Afnan lives in Abha. She is nine years old. She likes painting and reading. She visits us every summer. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence · 1.5] I always enjoy my time with Afnan. — The closing sentence returns to Afnan with a feeling.","h":"الخاتمة تعود إلى أفنان."},{"n":13,"s":"Which group of words is a complete sentence?","o":["The children in the yard.","Playing in the yard.","When the children play in the yard.","The children are playing in the yard."],"k":3,"e":"[error · 1.1] The children are playing in the yard. — Subject (The children) + verb (are playing).","h":"فاعل وفعل."},{"n":14,"s":"I (A) wanted to go (B) out, (C) and my mother (D) said no.","o":["wanted","out","and","said"],"k":2,"e":"[error · 1.3] and — Wanting to go out and the mother saying no is a contrast: but.","h":"التضاد يحتاج but."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Saudi Arabia has a big desert. (2) It is called the Empty Quarter. (3) It is very hot in summer. (4) Pizza is an Italian food. (5) Few people live there."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 1.6] Sentence 4 — Pizza is off the topic of the desert.","h":"البيتزا خارج موضوع الصحراء."},{"n":16,"s":"(A) Its very (B) hot (C) today, so (D) drink water.","o":["Its","hot","today","drink"],"k":0,"e":"[error · 1.4] Its — it is in short form is it's.","h":"الاختصار it's."},{"n":17,"s":"I (A) go (B) usually to (C) bed (D) at ten.","o":["go","usually","bed","at ten"],"k":1,"e":"[error · 1.2] usually — usually comes before the main verb: I usually go to bed.","h":"usually قبل الفعل."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My mornings are always busy.","The school bus is yellow.","Breakfast is very important.","I like the evening."],"x":["______ First, I pray Fajr. Then I have a quick breakfast. After that, I take the bus to school."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 1.5] My mornings are always busy. — The steps describe a morning routine.","h":"الخطوات تصف الصباح."},{"n":19,"s":"When I (A) was young, (B) i (C) lived (D) in Hail.","o":["was","i","lived","in"],"k":1,"e":"[error · 1.1] i — The word I is always a capital letter.","h":"الضمير I بحرف كبير دائمًا."},{"n":20,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["but","so","because","or"],"x":["My sister is sick, ______ she isn't going to school today."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector · 1.3] so — Not going to school is the result.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج so."},{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["It is brown and very friendly.","My uncle has a fast car.","Some people are afraid of cats.","The street is very long."],"x":["Our neighbours have a big dog. ______ It plays with the children in the street. Everyone likes it."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 1.6] It is brown and very friendly. — The missing sentence describes the dog, like the sentences around it.","h":"الجملة الناقصة تصف الكلب."},{"n":22,"s":"Which sentence uses an apostrophe correctly?","o":["I cant' find my keys.","I ca'nt find my keys.","I cant find my key's.","I can't find my keys."],"k":3,"e":"[error · 1.4] I can't find my keys. — The apostrophe replaces the missing letters: can't.","h":"الفاصلة العليا مكان الحروف المحذوفة."},{"n":23,"s":"Which question has the correct word order?","o":["What time does the film start?","What time the film starts?","What time starts the film?","The film starts what time?"],"k":0,"e":"[error · 1.2] What time does the film start? — Question word + does + subject + verb.","h":"أداة الاستفهام ثم does ثم الفاعل ثم الفعل."},{"n":24,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Banks open at nine.","Riyadh has many banks.","My father works hard, but he always has time for us.","I don't like homework."],"x":["My father works in a bank in Riyadh. He leaves home at seven every morning. He comes back at four. In the evening, he plays with us and helps us with our homework. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence · 1.5] My father works hard, but he always has time for us. — The closing sentence sums up both parts: hard work and time for the family.","h":"الخاتمة تجمع فكرتي العمل والوقت للأسرة."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["Are many shops in our street.","There many shops in our street.","there are many shops in our street.","There are many shops in our street."],"k":3,"e":"[error · 1.1] There are many shops in our street. — There + are + noun, with a capital letter.","h":"There ثم are ثم الاسم."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence correctly joins 'I was thirsty.' and 'I drank some water.'?","o":["I was thirsty, but I drank some water.","I was thirsty because I drank some water.","I was thirsty, so I drank some water.","I was thirsty, or I drank some water."],"k":2,"e":"[error · 1.3] I was thirsty, so I drank some water. — Drinking is the result of being thirsty: so.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج so."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Reading is my favourite hobby. (2) My brother is good at swimming. (3) I read every night before bed. (4) I like stories about animals. (5) I borrow books from the school library. (6) Reading makes me happy."],"k":0,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 1.6] Sentence 2 — The brother's swimming is off the topic of the writer's reading.","h":"سباحة الأخ خارج موضوع القراءة."},{"n":28,"s":"We (A) bought (B) shirt's, shoes (C) and hats (D) for Eid.","o":["bought","shirt's","and","for"],"k":1,"e":"[error · 1.4] shirt's — shirts is a plural: no apostrophe.","h":"الجمع بلا فاصلة عليا."},{"n":29,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["4 – 2 – 3 – 1","4 – 3 – 2 – 1","2 – 4 – 3 – 1","4 – 2 – 1 – 3"],"x":["(1) every morning","(2) walks","(3) to school","(4) Hamad"],"k":0,"e":"[best order · 1.2] 4 – 2 – 3 – 1 — Hamad walks to school every morning: place before time.","h":"المكان قبل الزمان."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["A hospital is a very important place.","Doctors study for many years.","My uncle is a nurse.","I was sick yesterday."],"x":["______ It is a big building with many rooms. Sick people go there to see a doctor. Nurses work there day and night."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 1.5] A hospital is a very important place. — All the details describe a hospital.","h":"التفاصيل تصف المستشفى."},{"n":31,"s":"(A) My best (B) friend (C) from (D) Egypt.","o":["My","friend","from","Egypt"],"k":2,"e":"[error · 1.1] from — The verb is is missing: My best friend is from Egypt.","h":"ينقص الفعل is."},{"n":32,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so","but","because","or"],"x":["We can take the bus ______ we can walk."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector · 1.3] or — Two choices are joined with or.","h":"خياران يحتاجان or."},{"n":33,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) My little brother loves trains. (2) He has many toy trains. (3) He reads books about trains. (4) He watches train videos. (5) He wants to be a train driver. (6) My mother bought new curtains."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 1.6] Sentence 6 — The curtains are off the topic of the brother's love of trains.","h":"الستائر خارج موضوع القطارات."},{"n":34,"s":"Which sentence is punctuated correctly?","o":["My friends are Saad Rayan and Turki.","My friends, are Saad, Rayan and Turki.","My friends are Saad, Rayan and Turki.","My friends are, Saad, Rayan and, Turki."],"k":2,"e":"[error · 1.4] My friends are Saad, Rayan and Turki. — Commas go between the names in the list.","h":"الفواصل بين الأسماء."},{"n":35,"s":"There (A) is (B) a cat black (C) under (D) the car.","o":["is","a cat black","under","the"],"k":1,"e":"[error · 1.2] a cat black — The adjective comes before the noun: a black cat.","h":"الصفة قبل الاسم."},{"n":36,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Coins are made of metal.","It was an interesting and useful trip.","The guide was tall.","My phone takes good photos."],"x":["Our class went to a museum last week. We saw old coins and swords. A guide told us about the history of our country. We took many photos. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence · 1.5] It was an interesting and useful trip. — The closing sentence gives an opinion about the whole trip.","h":"الخاتمة رأي في الرحلة كلها."},{"n":37,"s":"(A) We stayed (B) inside (C) so it (D) was raining.","o":["We","inside","so","was"],"k":2,"e":"[error · 1.3] so — The rain is the reason: because.","h":"السبب يحتاج because."},{"n":38,"s":"Which sentence is complete and correct?","o":["Last night, we ate dinner at my uncle's house.","Last night, ate dinner at my uncle's house.","Last night, we dinner at my uncle's house.","last night, we ate dinner at my uncle's house."],"k":0,"e":"[error · 1.1] Last night, we ate dinner at my uncle's house. — It has a capital letter, a subject (we) and a verb (ate).","h":"حرف كبير وفاعل وفعل."},{"n":39,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Supermarkets sell many things.","Sunday is a school day.","I like my bedroom.","My father washes the car."],"x":["Saturday is a busy day in our house. My mother goes to the supermarket. ______ My sisters and I tidy our rooms."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 1.6] My father washes the car. — The missing sentence tells what another family member does on Saturday.","h":"الجملة الناقصة عمل فرد آخر يوم السبت."},{"n":40,"s":"(A) Who's (B) bag is (C) this? Is it (D) yours?","o":["Who's","bag","this","yours"],"k":0,"e":"[error · 1.4] Who's — To ask about belonging, we use whose; who's means who is.","h":"whose للملكية وwho's بمعنى who is."},{"n":41,"s":"Which sentence has the correct word order?","o":["My mother drinks never coffee at night.","Never my mother drinks coffee at night.","My mother never drinks coffee at night.","My mother drinks coffee never at night."],"k":2,"e":"[error · 1.2] My mother never drinks coffee at night. — never comes before the main verb drinks.","h":"never قبل الفعل الرئيس."},{"n":42,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["There are many good things to do without a phone.","Phones are very expensive.","My family is big.","Drawing needs coloured pencils."],"x":["______ For example, you can talk to your family. You can also read or draw. Sometimes, a short walk is the best."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 1.5] There are many good things to do without a phone. — The examples are activities without a phone.","h":"الأمثلة أنشطة بلا هاتف."},{"n":43,"s":"He (A) practised every day, (B) but he (C) won the (D) race.","o":["practised","but","won","race"],"k":1,"e":"[error · 1.3] but — Winning is the result of practising: so.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج so."},{"n":44,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6","Sentence 7"],"x":["(1) Dates are an important food in Saudi Arabia. (2) Farmers grow many kinds of dates. (3) The best dates come from Al-Qassim and Al-Madinah. (4) People eat them with coffee. (5) Coffee shops are very busy at night. (6) Dates are also used in cakes and sweets. (7) Dates are healthy and full of energy."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 1.6] Sentence 5 — Sentence 5 is about coffee shops, not dates, even though sentence 4 mentions coffee.","h":"الجملة الخامسة عن المقاهي لا عن التمر."},{"n":45,"s":"After the (A) match, the (B) players (C) very tired and (D) hungry.","o":["match","players","very","hungry"],"k":2,"e":"[error · 1.1] very — The verb were is missing: the players were very tired.","h":"ينقص الفعل were."},{"n":46,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 4 – 1 – 5","2 – 4 – 3 – 1 – 5","3 – 2 – 4 – 1 – 5","1 – 2 – 3 – 4 – 5"],"x":["(1) in the garden","(2) My grandmother","(3) always","(4) sits","(5) after lunch"],"k":0,"e":"[best order · 1.2] 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 – 5 — My grandmother always sits in the garden after lunch.","h":"always قبل الفعل، والمكان قبل الزمان."},{"n":47,"s":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["The cat is playing with it's ball.","The cat is playing with its' ball.","The cat is playing with it ball.","The cat is playing with its ball."],"k":3,"e":"[error · 1.4] The cat is playing with its ball. — its = belonging to it; it's = it is.","h":"its للملكية وit's بمعنى it is."},{"n":48,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["My grandfather's stories help us learn about the past.","Fish is good for our health.","Jeddah has a big port today.","Small boats are not safe."],"x":["Many years ago, my grandfather was a fisherman in Jeddah. He went to sea in a small boat. He caught fish and sold them at the market. Today, he tells us stories about the sea. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence · 1.5] My grandfather's stories help us learn about the past. — The closing sentence connects the past and the stories today.","h":"الخاتمة تربط الماضي بالقصص اليوم."},{"n":49,"s":"Which sentence uses the connector correctly?","o":["I didn't go to the party, so I had a test the next day.","I didn't go to the party, or I had a test the next day.","I didn't go to the party, and because I had a test the next day.","I didn't go to the party because I had a test the next day."],"k":3,"e":"[error · 1.3] I didn't go to the party because I had a test the next day. — The test is the reason for not going: because.","h":"الاختبار هو السبب."},{"n":50,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Learning English is useful for students. (2) It helps them read books from other countries. (3) Many students in my class wear glasses. (4) It also helps them use the internet. (5) In the future, it can help them find good jobs. (6) That is why English is an important subject."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 1.6] Sentence 3 — Glasses are off the topic of learning English.","h":"النظارات خارج موضوع تعلم الإنجليزية."}]}],"n":50}};
